@startuml direct-rialto-lifecycle-play-hold-activity
title AampRialtoPlaybackController: evaluate after RequestPlay / AddHold / ReleaseHold

start
:take m_playMutex (recursive);
:take m_mutex;
:apply the operation\n(set request, add or clear hold bit);
note right
  AddHold always leaves holds != 0, so it can
  never issue play(), but it can start pre-roll.
  Reset() restores the initial holds without
  dispatching anything.
end note
if (play request pending\nand holds == 0?) then (yes)
  :consume the request\n(m_playPending = false);
  :release m_mutex;
  :IssuePlay(): ungate sources, play();
  stop
elseif (play request pending and\nholds == PreRollIncomplete only?) then (yes)
  if (new pre-roll episode?) then (yes)
    :++episode;
    :release m_mutex;
    :unlock one level of m_playMutex;
    :StartPreRoll(episode):\npause(), ungate, start monitor;
    :relock m_playMutex;
  else (no)
    :release m_mutex;
  endif
  stop
else (no)
  :release m_mutex;
  :nothing to do;
  stop
endif
note right
  Pre-roll steps run through RunIfPreRollCurrent(episode),
  so a stale pre-roll (episode ended by Flush, Configure
  or Stop) can neither ungate nor release a re-armed hold.
end note
@enduml
